\phi(A) = 0.42, \quad \phi(B) = 0.08, \quad \phi(C) = -0.50

Ranking: A > B > C. The non-compensatory method agrees with the geometric mean in ranking A first but provides more information about the magnitude of differences.

Note: These are theoretical calculations demonstrating the formal properties of non-compensatory aggregation. They are not empirical measurements of actual civilizations.

