Caption: The Gaussian copula (left) exhibits asymptotically independent tails; the joint probability of extreme events in both margins approaches zero faster than the marginal tail probability. The Student-t copula with finite degrees of freedom (right) exhibits positive tail dependence, with a non-negligible probability mass in the joint upper tail. The tail dependence coefficient \lambda is zero for the Gaussian copula and positive for the Student-t copula, as derived in Appendix A.1.

