9. ADICO Institutional Grammar Syntax

This diagram shows the structural decomposition of an institutional statement into ADICO components.

```
   Institutional Statement:
   "States Parties must notify WHO of events that may constitute
    a public health emergency of international concern within 24 hours."

   ADICO decomposition:
   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │  A (Attribute)  :  States Parties                          │
   │  D (Deontic)    :  MUST                                    │
   │  I (Aim)        :  notify WHO of events...                 │
   │  C (Condition)  :  within 24 hours of assessment           │
   │  O (Or else)    :  NONE (no formal sanction)               │
   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Structural classification: NORM (lacks "Or else" component)
```

Caption: The ADICO grammar decomposes an institutional rule into five components. The presence or absence of the "Or else" (sanction) distinguishes full rules from norms. This coding scheme enables systematic comparison of institutional design across domains (Chapter 5).

